  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Emergency Appeal 2025 for Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Yemen&#x2019;s ongoing conflict and economic collapse have left 19.5 million people in need of humanitarian assistance. This project aims to support 174,667 vulnerable women, men, girls, and boys in selected districts of Aden and Hadramout with lifesaving Health and WASH services.

The project supports five health facilities in Aden and Hadramout to provide life-saving primary health, nutrition, and WASH services for 174,667 vulnerable people. Activities include supplying medical equipment and PPE, supporting health workers, improving service quality, strengthening obstetric and newborn care, and ensuring safe referrals. WASH upgrades include rehabilitating water systems, sanitation, and waste management, and ensuring safe drinking water in line with IPC and cholera-prevention standards. All interventions follow MSP, SPHERE and protection guidelines, include strong community feedback mechanisms, and are coordinated with clusters and local authorities to ensure quality, accountability and support to at-risk communities.</narrative>
  </description>
